  "details": "People do a lot of tiny movements when they want to get close to someone/something. A lot of the time, they over-correct because they move too much when trying to slowly deflect the stick. I propose changing the curve from linear to an S-curve.\n\nThis is **NOT** the same as movement acceleration. That, in turn, acts after the input has been done and causes motion sickness. This is simply changing the curve that the thumbsticks actuate on.\n\n**Deploy the diagram!:**",
